cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "dyadmocap-temporal-mapper: Temporal Mapper analysis of dyadic motion capture"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, in Python and MATLAB, for studying how two seated people's
  body movements are organised over a conversation, using the Temporal Mapper
  on dyadic motion-capture data, and comparing a casual chat with a conflict
  conversation. Runs on simulated dyads; the study's recordings are not public.
authors:
  - family-names: Akatuhwera
    given-names: Patience
    affiliation: "Multiscale Complex Systems Lab, Michigan State University"
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pesh282/dyadmocap-temporal-mapper"
keywords:
  - temporal mapper
  - motion capture
  - dyadic interaction
  - nonverbal behaviour
  - topological data analysis
